# 06-saga run 2026-09-27T19:21:15Z
== fresh Postgres with one database per service (docker compose down -v && up) ==
 Container 06-saga-postgres-1 Healthy 
setup: 4 databases (inventory, payments, shipping, orchestrator), keyboard stock = 10
== demo (the process is killed in scenario 4) ==

## 1. Happy path
   concept: three local transactions in three databases, one after another; the saga log records progress after each
   [order-A] started {"sku":"keyboard","qty":2,"amount":"84.00","address":"Paris"}
   [order-A] step 1 reserveInventory: ok
   [order-A] step 2 chargePayment: ok
   [order-A] step 3 createShipment: ok
   [order-A] completed

## 2. Payment fails
   concept: no distributed rollback exists; the orchestrator undoes completed steps with compensating actions, in reverse
   [order-B] started {"sku":"keyboard","qty":1,"amount":"5000.00","address":"Paris"}
   [order-B] step 1 reserveInventory: ok
   [order-B] step 2 chargePayment: FAILED (card declined for 5000.00) -> compensate 1 completed step(s)
   [order-B] compensate reserveInventory: ok
   [order-B] aborted

## 3. Last step fails
   concept: shipping refuses: refund the charge, then release the stock
   [order-C] started {"sku":"keyboard","qty":3,"amount":"126.00","address":"nowhere"}
   [order-C] step 1 reserveInventory: ok
   [order-C] step 2 chargePayment: ok
   [order-C] step 3 createShipment: FAILED (address not deliverable: nowhere) -> compensate 2 completed step(s)
   [order-C] compensate chargePayment: ok
   [order-C] compensate reserveInventory: ok
   [order-C] aborted

## 4. Orchestrator crashes mid-saga
   concept: the charge ran but the log was not updated; the process dies here (resume picks it up)
   [order-D] started {"sku":"keyboard","qty":1,"amount":"42.00","address":"Lyon"}
   [order-D] step 1 reserveInventory: ok
   [order-D] step 2 chargePayment: ok
   [order-D] CRASH after chargePayment ran, before the saga log recorded it
demo exited with 1
== proof: saga log right after the crash (order-D stuck at step 1 although its charge exists) ==
   id    |   state   | step |              error               
---------+-----------+------+----------------------------------
 order-A | completed |    3 | 
 order-B | aborted   |    0 | card declined for 5000.00
 order-C | aborted   |    0 | address not deliverable: nowhere
 order-D | running   |    1 | 
(4 rows)

 saga_id | amount | status  
---------+--------+---------
 order-D |  42.00 | charged
(1 row)

== resume in a new process ==

## 5. Recovery
   concept: on restart, the orchestrator reloads unfinished sagas from its log and continues; steps are idempotent (keyed by saga id), so re-running chargePayment does not charge twice
   [order-D] found running at step 1, resuming
   [order-D] step 2 chargePayment: ok
   [order-D] step 3 createShipment: ok
   [order-D] completed

== proof: saga log ==
